# {{ project_name }} — Spec Schema

> This document defines the **required format** for every artifact in the spec tree.
> Automated validators and CoCo hooks enforce these rules.

---

## 1. Decision Records (`decisions/NNN-slug.md`)

### Frontmatter (YAML)

```yaml
---
id: ADR-NNN          # unique, zero-padded 3-digit number
title: "<title>"     # concise imperative sentence
date: YYYY-MM-DD     # ISO 8601
status: <status>     # see valid statuses below
---
```

**Valid statuses:** `proposed` | `accepted` | `deprecated` | `superseded`

### Required Sections

| Section         | Description                                      |
|-----------------|--------------------------------------------------|
| **Context**     | Why is this decision needed? What forces are at play? |
| **Decision**    | What was decided and why this option was chosen.  |
| **Consequences**| Trade-offs, follow-up work, risks introduced.     |

---

## 2. Proposal Files (`proposals/NNN-slug.md`)

### Frontmatter (YAML)

```yaml
---
id: EXT-NNN          # unique, zero-padded 3-digit number
title: "<title>"
phase: <phase>       # integer phase number (1, 2, 3, ...)
status: <status>     # see valid statuses below
depends_on: []       # list of EXT-NNN or ADR-NNN ids
promoted_to: MOD-NN  # optional — set when this proposal becomes a module
---
```

**Valid statuses:** `planned` | `in-progress` | `implemented` | `cancelled` | `parked`

### Required Sections

| Section               | Description                                    |
|-----------------------|------------------------------------------------|
| **Problem Statement** | What's broken or missing, and why it matters.  |
| **Summary**           | What this proposal adds or changes.            |
| **Prerequisites**     | What must be true before work begins.          |
| **Scope**             | Explicit in-scope / out-of-scope boundaries.   |

### Batch Cleanup Proposals

For non-behavioral changes that batch 3+ small items (test coverage, dead code removal, typo fixes), a reduced format is acceptable:

**Qualifying criteria (all must be true):**
- Non-behavioral: no change to inputs, outputs, or observable behavior
- No `impacts_modules` entries (or empty list)
- 3 or more distinct items batched together
- No new dependencies or infrastructure changes

**Reduced format:**
- **Problem Statement**: Single sentence summarizing the category of cleanup
- **Scope**: Bulleted list of items (no in-scope/out-of-scope separation needed)
- **Acceptance Criteria**: Checklist style (numbered items, each verifiable by inspection or test run)

**Omitted sections:** Prerequisites, Summary (scope IS the summary for batch cleanups)

**Canonical example:** EXT-034 ("Code health cleanup")

Regular proposals remain the default. Batch format is opt-in — use only when all qualifying criteria are met.

